Every finding MUST have `file_line` (a real `path:line`) OR `deferred: true`
with a `deferred_reason`. Gate B rejects any finding missing both. `severity`
MUST be exactly one of: critical, high, medium, low, info. Never fabricate.

## Gate B repair

If `gate_defects` is present in context (Gate B found structural defects —
empty track, bad severity, missing citation), re-run this template with
`gate_defects` in context and re-emit the corrected `findings` and
`defense_layer_coverage`. Never fabricate a `file_line`; if you cannot cite a
real line, mark the finding `deferred: true` with a `deferred_reason`. If the
surface genuinely has no findings, emit a single `id: "KS-00"`, `severity:
"info"`, `title: "no findings on <surface>"`, `file_line: "<scope root>:0"`
finding so the track is non-empty.